# Pairs with SplitCompletes. Production before #4264: a split whose copy an
# alias move retargets has no way out. Since #4478 a split may run on the
# resized copy while its resize can still be undone, so an undo that moves the
# alias back to the old copy leaves the split with every coordinator step
# disabled (each requires the tree to resolve to the split's copy).
# TreeShardSplitGrain.AbandonRetargetedSplitAsync, the base's SplitAbandon, is
# what lets it finish. A second edit lets the stranded split count as
# quiescent, so the mutant cannot deadlock and the liveness property is the
# only thing TLC can report.
MODULE: SplitCompletesUndoWithoutAbandon
TARGET: SplitCompletes
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a split of the resized copy an undo retargets is never abandoned, so it never completes
PERTURBS: SplitAbandon

--- FIND
    /\ alias # spCopy
    /\ sp' = "done"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a retargeted split is never abandoned.
    /\ FALSE
    /\ sp' = "done"
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"}
--- REPLACE
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
\* MUTATION: a split the undo stranded counts as quiescent.
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"} \/ alias # spCopy
--- END